{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1782568464,"nonce":"r2t6FdA0/lVpTW8QILpuNVcRWJE=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABHy6xCg","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/339#issuecomment-4818120970"},"message":"Related prior issue: #138 (mru_transform: choose durable nav-input source — from the 2026-05-19 ellipsoidal-vs-EKF discovery) tracks the **same nav-source decision**. The operator's standing lean is to **keep the FCU as primary nav source**; this issue's SBG-primary direction should be weighed against that rather than duplicating it — linking for consolidation. New evidence here from the 2026-06-26 gyro fault (FCU EKF attitude *and* altitude diverged while the SBG stayed solid) is the relevant input to that decision.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null},{"type":3,"timestamp":1782573476,"nonce":"Ohd7GiAgAJ/OLZu588K4WTyqGg8=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABHzfjnw","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/339#issuecomment-4818723743"},"message":"## Handoff for the gabby agent (live-data work)\n\nBranch **`feature/issue-339`** has the staging done; the remaining `mru_transform` source rewire is left for you to apply and validate against live boat data.\n\n### Already committed on `feature/issue-339`\n- `urdf(bizzyboat)`: added SBG antenna frames `sbg_gnss_primary` (−1.073, 0, 0.8825, aft — where `gps_pos`/`imu/nav_sat_fix` report) and `sbg_gnss_secondary` (0.973, 0, 0.88, fwd). Also corrected the **M3 transducer face** (−0.23, 0, −0.145) → (−0.29, 0, −0.28) (the old z was ~half the true depth = 13.5 cm sounding bias).\n- `config(sbg)`: `use_enu: true` (required — the driver gates *all* `ros_standard` publishers on it) and `frame_id: \"bizzy/sbg_gnss_primary\"`.\n\n### Remaining change — apply to `bizzyboat.yaml` `/**/mru_transform`\n```yaml\nsensors:\n  sbg:                                       # NEW — primary\n    topics:\n      orientation: \"sensors/imu/data\"        # SBG ENU attitude (use_enu:true)\n      position:    \"sensors/imu/nav_sat_fix\"  # SBG primary antenna, ellipsoidal\n      velocity:    \"sensors/imu/velocity\"     # SBG ENU velocity\n  mru:                                        # FCU — fallback\n    topics:\n      orientation: \"mavros/imu/data\"\n      position:    \"mavros/global_position/global\"\n      velocity:    \"mavros/local_position/velocity_body\"\nsensor_names: [sbg, mru]                       # was [mru]\nsensor_timeout: 0.5                            # failover window — tune live\n```\n\n### Why this design (context)\n- `mru_transform` uses the orientation quaternion **directly** as `base_link` attitude and only rotates the gyro by `frame_id`; `PositionSensor` uses `frame_id`'s static TF to offset the fix to `base_link`. Because `sbg_gnss_primary` has identity rotation vs `base_link`, the single driver `frame_id` serves both position (antenna lever arm) and orientation/gyro (identity) — **provided the SBG output is vehicle-axis-aligned**.\n- Antenna geometry cross-checks 3 ways to ~3–6 cm: your tape measurements, the SBG flash lever arms (baseline 2.05 m), and an independent GPS baseline estimate (FCU − SBG_primary = 1.843 m fwd).\n\n### Boat-side verification checklist (the reason this is live work)\n1. **Standard topics publish**: with `use_enu:true`, confirm `ros2 topic list` shows `/bizzy/sensors/imu/data`, `/imu/nav_sat_fix`, `/imu/velocity` (they were absent before — `use_enu:false` blocked them).\n2. **Attitude alignment** (the key assumption): `imu/data` attitude matches known heading / the FCU on a clean run, with **no residual mounting rotation**. If there is one, split into a real `sbg_imu` frame + a relay re-stamping `imu/nav_sat_fix` to `sbg_gnss_primary` (the single-frame trick only holds when aligned).\n3. **No fallback jump**: force/observe SBG↔FCU failover and confirm `base_link` position doesn't jump (both should land within a few cm). `nav/active_sensor/*` shows the live source.\n4. **Vertical datum unchanged**: `map_tide` z stays ~48.8 m (ellipsoidal); `imu/nav_sat_fix` = `altitude + undulation`, so it's already ellipsoidal.\n5. Re-check `sensor_timeout` against real SBG/FCU rates (50 / ~10 Hz).\n\nNote the arbitration is \"newest fresh sample wins, priority breaks ties\" — at 50 Hz the SBG dominates while healthy and FCU only takes over on real dropout. If strict primary-preference is wanted, that's a small `updateLatest` change.\n\nThe branch is pushed to gitcloud for pickup. Decoupling nav from the FCU also removes the gyro-fault exposure (#337 — FCU EKF attitude *and* altitude diverge under the failed gyro).\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}